## TLDR Problem this solves: - OTel metrics shipped `gen_ai.system` as `None` - Exporter rejected it and logged a stack trace - Rejection repeated every export cycle, forever - Same raw provider value went onto content events How it solves it: - Drop the provider label when there is none - Applies to metrics, content events, inference-details event - Matches what the v2 OTel integration already does ## User Flow Before: a platform team pointing the proxy at their OTel collector gets a stack trace in the gateway logs every minute after any Anthropic Messages, Responses, streaming, or passthrough call, and it never stops 1. The admin runs the proxy with `callbacks: ["otel"]`, `LITELLM_OTEL_INTEGRATION_ENABLE_METRICS=true` and `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` set to their collector 2. A developer sends POST https://litellm-domain/v1/messages with `{"model": "claude-opus-5", "max_tokens": 16, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi"}]}` and gets 200 with a normal completion 3. Within a minute the gateway logs `ERROR ... Failed to encode key gen_ai.system: Invalid type <class 'NoneType'> of value None` with a full stack trace 4. Nobody sends anything else, and the same error keeps appearing every minute, so the team's log bill grows on an idle gateway 5. Their dashboards never get a provider breakdown for those calls After: the same calls stay 200 and the gateway logs stay clean, with metrics carrying a provider label whenever the call has one 1. The admin runs the proxy with the same config 2. The developer sends the same POST https://litellm-domain/v1/messages and gets 200 with a normal completion 3. No encoding error appears in the gateway logs, then or on any later export 4. The gateway sits idle without producing new errors 5. Dashboards keep the provider breakdown for calls that carry a provider, and calls without one simply have no provider label instead of a broken series ## Relevant issues Fixes #36759 ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [ ] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Two proxies were run side by side against the real Anthropic API, one at the base commit `7fcca523aab19dbd5d4d5b5ff9a057d0110ecaaa` and one at this PR's tip `7d70d3c045`, both with the config from the issue plus a collector endpoint, on ports 51401 and 51402 ``` $ cat repro-config.yaml model_list: - model_name: claude-opus-5 litellm_params: model: anthropic/claude-opus-5 api_key: os.environ/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY litellm_settings: callbacks: - otel json_logs: true callback_settings: otel: message_logging: true $ OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp \ OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317 \ LITELLM_OTEL_INTEGRATION_ENABLE_METRICS=true LITELLM_OTEL_INTEGRATION_ENABLE_EVENTS=true \ litellm --config repro-config.yaml --detailed_debug --port 51401 > before.log 2>&1 ``` The same five user calls were sent to each proxy, all real spend, all 200 on both ``` $ for P in 51401 51402; do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$P chat %{http_code}
" http://localhost:$P/v1/chat/completions \ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-...' \ -d '{"model":"claude-opus-5","max_tokens":16,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}' curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$P messages %{http_code}
" http://localhost:$P/v1/messages \ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-...' \ -d '{"model":"claude-opus-5","max_tokens":16,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}' curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$P responses %{http_code}
" http://localhost:$P/v1/responses \ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-...' \ -d '{"model":"claude-opus-5","input":"hi"}' curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$P stream %{http_code}
" http://localhost:$P/v1/chat/completions \ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-...' \ -d '{"model":"claude-opus-5","max_tokens":16,"stream":true,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}' curl -s -o /dev/null -w "$P passthrough %{http_code}
" http://localhost:$P/anthropic/v1/messages \ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-...' -H 'anthropic-version: 2023-06-01' \ -d '{"model":"claude-opus-5","max_tokens":16,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}' done 51401 chat 200 51401 messages 200 51401 responses 200 51401 stream 200 51401 passthrough 200 51402 chat 200 51402 messages 200 51402 responses 200 51402 stream 200 51402 passthrough 200 ``` Base commit `7fcca523aa`, the customer symptom, growing with each export cycle while the gateway sits idle ``` $ grep -c 'Failed to encode key gen_ai.system' before.log 60 $ sleep 130; grep -c 'Failed to encode key gen_ai.system' before.log 120 $ grep -m1 'Failed to encode key gen_ai.system' before.log {"message": "Failed to encode key gen_ai.system: Invalid type <class 'NoneType'> of value None", "level": "ERROR", "timestamp": "2026-08-13T20:09:08.036060", "component": "opentelemetry.exporter.otlp.proto.common._internal", "logger": "__init__.py:115", "stacktrace": "Traceback (most recent call last):
