## TLDR Problem this solves: - Vertex pass-through returned a bare "Internal server error" - Google credential failures gave callers no hint what to fix How it solves it: - Catch credential failures on the pass-through route - Return 401 naming project, location, and the Google error - Let transport failures keep propagating, so they are not mislabeled as auth ## User Flow Before: a developer calling Gemini through the gateway's Vertex pass-through route gets an opaque 500 and cannot tell whether the fault is theirs or the gateway's 1. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "gemini-2.5-flash"` and get a normal 200 with a completion 2. They send the equivalent native call, POST https://litellm-domain/vertex_ai/v1/projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/publishers/google/models/gemini-2.5-flash:generateContent with a `contents` array 3. They get back HTTP 500 with `{"error": {"message": "Internal server error", "type": "internal_server_error"}}` 4. Nothing in the response says which project the gateway tried, that Google refused to issue a token, or what the admin should configure, so they file a ticket After: the same call comes back as a 401 that names the project, the region, and Google's own reason, so the admin fixes it without a ticket 1. They send POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions with `"model": "gemini-2.5-flash"` and get a normal 200 with a completion 2. They send the same POST https://litellm-domain/vertex_ai/v1/projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/publishers/google/models/gemini-2.5-flash:generateContent with a `contents` array 3. They now get HTTP 401 with `"Failed to get a Google access token for project=my-project + location=us-central1: Your default credentials were not found..."` plus a pointer to set `vertex_credentials` on the deployment marked `use_in_pass_through: true`, or on `default_vertex_config` 4. The admin adds the missing service-account credentials, and the same call returns Google's native `candidates` payload with HTTP 200 ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [ ] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix Live proxy against real Vertex AI, config with a pass-through project/location whose credentials are not resolvable on the pod (`default_vertex_config` project + location, no service account), while a `model_list` deployment carries its own `vertex_credentials` so `/v1/chat/completions` keeps working. Before, at 87736a767c: ``` $ curl -s -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
" http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions \ -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-1234' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"model":"gemini-2.5-flash","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"say hi in 3 words"}]}' {"id":"lkJ-au2bM9qCwLUPkZfcEA", ... "choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"Hello there!","role":"assistant"}}], "usage":{"completion_tokens":29,"prompt_tokens":6,"total_tokens":35}} HTTP 200 $ curl -s -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
