" http://localhost:24688/v1/chat/completions \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Reply with exactly: chat-ok"}],"max_tokens":16}' HTTP 200 content: chat-ok usage: 20 total tokens /v1/messages -> HTTP 200 content: messages-ok /v1/responses -> HTTP 200 output: responses-ok /v1/embeddings -> HTTP 200 1024-dim embedding ``` The after leg ran in a worktree that additionally carried the pending dashboard `schema.d.ts` regeneration, which is types-only and cannot change proxy behavior QA observations: - /v1/messages never leaked; 200 on both legs - Titan reports the leak as three schema violations - Live batch execution itself is exercised in #36634 ## Type 🐛 Bug Fix ## Caveats (if any) - `bedrock_tags` and `s3_output_bucket_name` registered but untested live - Only the five documented Bedrock batch fields are covered ### Final Attestation - [x] The tests check the right things, including the edge cases, and regressions in the respective real-world customer use-cases are not possible after this PR <!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY --> --- > [!NOTE] > <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 3312f0beeac1e47c2093367edc06e5ef981bce41. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup> <!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->

## TLDR Problem this solves: - NIM/vLLM clients send extras Fireworks names differently or historically rejected - The legacy `/v1/completions` path 500'd on `reasoning_effort` and `response_format` How it solves it: - Translates truncate, reasoning, and guided-decoding extras to Fireworks-native params - Strips extras with no Fireworks equivalent, with a debug log - On conflicts the Fireworks-native value silently wins, matching the Fireworks gateway - Applies the same translation on the text completion path, fixing its 500 - Drops `reasoning_effort: "auto"`; omitting it already means the model default ## User Flow Before: chat requests carry the NIM/vLLM knobs, but the legacy completions endpoint dies with a 500 inside the gateway 1. Point an existing NIM/vLLM OpenAI-compatible client at the gateway and send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions` with a Fireworks model, `truncate_prompt_tokens: 4096`, `chat_template_kwargs: {"enable_thinking": false}`, and a `guided_json` schema 2. The 200 reply honors the knobs: thinking is off and the content is valid JSON matching the schema (the Fireworks API accepts the NIM/vLLM names natively as of 2026-08-13; when this PR was opened they were ignored or rejected) 3. Send the NIM/vLLM knobs to the legacy `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/completions` with a `prompt` plus `reasoning_effort: "low"` and `best_of: 2`, and the call dies with `500 AsyncCompletions.create() got an unexpected keyword argument 'reasoning_effort'` before ever reaching Fireworks After: the same client works on both endpoints 1. Point an existing NIM/vLLM OpenAI-compatible client at the gateway and send `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/chat/completions` with a Fireworks model, `truncate_prompt_tokens: 4096`, `chat_template_kwargs: {"enable_thinking": false}`, and a `guided_json` schema 2. The 200 reply honors the knobs: thinking is off and the content is valid JSON matching the schema (now guaranteed by the gateway's own translation to the Fireworks-native names, not by the provider tolerating the NIM/vLLM ones) 3. The same legacy `POST https://litellm-domain/v1/completions` request returns 200 with the completion text ## Relevant issues ## Linear ticket Resolves LIT-5322 ## Pre-Submission checklist **Please complete all items before asking a LiteLLM maintainer to review your PR** - [x] I have added meaningful tests - [x] My PR passes all CI/CD checks (e.g., lint, format, unit tests) - [x] My PR's scope is as isolated as possible; it only solves 1 specific problem - [x] I have received a Greptile **Confidence Score of at least 4/5** before requesting a maintainer review (Greptile reviews automatically once the PR is opened; only comment `@greptileai` to re-request a review after pushing changes) ## Delays in PR merge? If you're seeing a delay in your PR being merged, ping the LiteLLM Team on [Slack (#pr-review)](https://join.slack.com/t/litellmossslack/shared_invite/zt-3o7nkuyfr-p_kbNJj8taRfXGgQI1~YyA). ## Screenshots / Proof of Fix QA run 2026-08-13, real Fireworks API calls. Before leg: proxy booted from `litellm_internal_staging` tip `9d069f21dc` (no PR). After leg: proxy booted from this PR's head `6b3977472b`. Both used the same config and the same curls: ```yaml model_list: - model_name: fw-glm litellm_params: model: fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/models/glm-5p2 - model_name: fw-oss litellm_params: model: fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/models/gpt-oss-120b ``` Step 1, chat completions with the NIM/vLLM knobs: ``` curl -s http://localhost:<port>/v1/chat/completions -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -d '{ "model": "fw-glm", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Greet me."}], "max_tokens": 2048, "truncate_prompt_tokens": 4096, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}, "guided_json": {"type": "object", "properties": {"greeting": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["greeting"]} }' ``` Before `9d069f21dc` (200, knobs honored natively by the Fireworks API, which forwards them verbatim): ```json {"id":"chatcmpl-be20817e633346ea934002077acb224a","created":1786679063,"model":"fw-glm","object":"chat.completion","choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"{
